# Motion

Animate `transform` and `opacity` only. Lenis lerp `0.1`, synced to the ScrollTrigger ticker. Lenis was not in the reference saves. It is an addition.

Easings taken from the study, used for the effect they belonged to:

- Arrows: `cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`, `1.6s` infinite (`main.css` `arrowIn` / `arrowOut`).
- Underline: `cubic-bezier(0, 0.55, 0.45, 1)`, `.4s` (`hoverLine`).
- Letter roll and Otsu ease-out: `cubic-bezier(.22, .61, .36, 1)`, `.32s`.
- Otsu `--ease`: `cubic-bezier(.16, 1, .3, 1)`. Hero image zoom uses it for `1.4s`.
- Cover fade-in: `cubic-bezier(.25, 1, .5, 1)`, `1.45s` with a `.5s` delay (`fadeInArea`).

GSAP default ease is `power3.out` where the reference did not name one. Page transitions take 500–700ms. Ambient loops that are not copied from a measured keyframe stay in the 4–8s range. `pillFloat` is the exception: `6s` ease-in-out, `translateY(-7px)`.

Do not install GSAP, Lenis, or SplitText until Phase 1 is approved. Build them in this repo.

The live home uses the Kamitsubaki motions only: ground swap, scroll line, and arrow loop. Reel and key effects stay in this note as study, and they are not on the page.

## Scroll catalogue

Build these as reusable hooks or components in `src/motion/` when Phase 1 starts.

1. `Reveal` — `sky`. Fade-up `1rem`, once. Start `top bottom-=30%`, end `bottom top+=70%`. CSS transition `.5s` (`linear` opacity, `ease-out` transform). The saved Kamitsubaki HTML never puts `.atg` on an element. The hook still comes from `main.min.js.download`.
2. `SplitHeadline` — `sky`. Chars from `y: 100%` to `0` with a slight rotate, `back.out(1.6)`, stagger `0.03s`. This stagger is not the Otsu letter roll.
3. `ParallaxLayer` — `sky`. `data-speed` on clouds, blobs, and glass, scrubbed.
4. `BgShift` — home. Sections with `data-bgchg` set `body[data-bg]` when they cross `top 50%` / `bottom 50%`. The pair is `#fcfcfc` / `#020202`.
5. `PinnedHorizontal` — `key` and illustration. Pin plus x translate. Nested reveals use `containerAnimation`.
6. `WipeReveal` — `key`. Cover `fadeAndPaint`: opacity 0 and `translateY(15%)`, then `background-position-x` from `100%` to `0`.
7. `FrameSequence` — animation page, any version. Canvas image sequence driven by scroll progress. No frame sequence was in `resource/`.
8. `VelocityMarquee` — `reel`. CSS marquee to `translate(-50%)`. Measured loops: `46s`, reverse `58s`, third row `40s`, and a separate `26s` track. Hover pauses. Reduced motion sets `animation: none`. GSAP may scale `timeScale` by scroll velocity on top of that.
9. `PortalZoom` — all versions, on the three portal cards. A pinned card scales to the viewport, then the route changes.
10. `KVSequence` — `key`. Three frames crossfade. Swiper speed on the Kamitsubaki sliders is `600`. Cover's key visual is Swiper markup. Staged lines are separate SVG files in the reference. Use text, not those SVGs.

## Interactions

- Letter-roll hover on the `reel` nav: each letter is doubled. Hover moves `translateY(-100%)` in `.32s` with stagger `0.018s`, and only for `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`.
- `hoverLine` on `sky`: underline `scaleX` over `.4s` with `cubic-bezier(0, 0.55, 0.45, 1)`.
- `reel` pills float `7px` over `6s` ease-in-out. Showreel controls are Unmute and Pause, at least 44px tall.
- Cursor glow on `key` only, from `768px` up, desktop pointer only. The reference circle is 116px and was not mounted in the saved HTML. Use a pastel orb, not the gray shadow.
- Heart or sparkle burst on click in `reel`, using `--dx`, `--dy`, and `--rot`, `.85s`. Reduced motion hides the particles.
- Route change: a glass curtain or bubble wipe via the View Transitions API, plus a top loading bar. Move focus to the new `h1`.

Video may autoplay only while muted and only when motion is allowed. Sound never autoplays. Players expose pause.

## Reduced motion and Calm mode

`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` and the in-site Calm mode toggle do the same thing:

- Turn off Lenis, scrub, pins, parallax, cursor effects, and marquees. Show marquees as a static grid.
- Content is visible immediately, with a simple 150ms opacity.
- Video does not autoplay.
- Pinned horizontal sections become swipe carousels.

Pinned sections stay in DOM order so keyboard and screen-reader users are not trapped.

## Mobile

Native touch scroll. Do not run Lenis on touch (`syncTouch: false` if it stays loaded). Pinned horizontal sections become swipe carousels. Blur is 10px, with at most 3 blobs. No cursor effects. Frame sequences are shorter.

## Performance

- At most about 6 `backdrop-filter` elements in one viewport.
- Initial route JS under 180 KB gzip. Lazy-load three/ogl, wavesurfer, and frame sequences.
- LCP under 2.5s, CLS under 0.05, INP under 200ms on mid-range mobile.
- Hold 60fps while scrolling.
- Hero video loops at 720–1080p and 4 MB or less, with a poster and `preload="metadata"`. Do not ship the 46 MB resource file as the reel.

## Home

One home, in the Kamitsubaki order. Centered text wordmark, tracked line, scroll cue, news on black, roster on white, discography squares on white. Reduced motion stops the scroll line and the arrows. The ground swap still happens. Do not point a hero at the 46866373-byte mp4.

News slider, when a version includes it: fraction labels padded to two digits (`01 / 05`), autoplay delay `5000`, speed `600`, progress width from time remaining. Jacket slider: 3 per view, speed `600`, delay `6000`. The saved pages do not implement a cover / original / unit filter. `mixitup.js` is loaded and never called. A filter on the Vsinger page is new work, not a copy of those files.
